## Context
Surfaced by the /verify gate on PR #268 (raid 219-224, ticket 0219).
0219 replaced the hardcoded `!= "main"` comparison in hookBody with
dynamic default-branch detection, and added a coherence guard that
byte-compares the installed hook against the integration.md snippet.
But tests/test_hook.sh and tests/test_roundtrip.sh carry independent
hand-rolled copies of the OLD `!= "main"` hook logic as hermetic
fixtures: they are not extracted from hookBody, so they still pass
and the new coherence guard does not cover them. They silently
diverge from the shipped hook behaviour.

## Actions
1. Decide per fixture: extract from hookBody (preferred, keeps them
   honest) or update the hand-rolled copy to the dynamic-detection
   form with a comment naming the divergence risk.
2. If extraction is feasible, route them through the same managed
   block used by the test_selfcoherence.sh guard (iv).

## Test
A grep for '"main"' (hardcoded literal in hook-shaped fixtures) over
tests/*.sh returns no hits outside the negative-control cases.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] test_hook.sh fixture matches shipped hookBody behaviour
- [ ] test_roundtrip.sh fixture matches shipped hookBody behaviour
- [ ] make check passes

## Imagine (raid 2026-06-04)
- Why now: 0219 replaced the hardcoded `!= "main"` guard with dynamic default-branch
  detection and added the erg validate/check section to hookBody, but the two shell
  fixtures were never updated. The drift is larger than the ticket title suggests:
  test_hook.sh's hand-rolled hook is missing the entire validate/check section and
  its error message text ("make build", "build/erg") no longer matches the shipped
  hook; test_roundtrip.sh carries the same truncated hook. Both now exercise logic
  that was never shipped.
- Scope check: two files (test_hook.sh, test_roundtrip.sh), two hand-rolled hook
  fragments. The two fixtures are asymmetric: test_roundtrip.sh already uses the
  real binary and tests install/uninstall round-trip, so replacing the cat heredoc
  with `$ERG install "$REPO" --hooks` is strictly more faithful. test_hook.sh is
  more involved: it uses an ELF stub for Tests 1-3, but Test 4 stages a .erg file
  and the real hook will exec `tickets/erg validate` -- the stub must be replaced
  with the real binary there, and Test 2's string assertions ("make build",
  "build/erg") must update to the shipped strings.
- Simplest path: for both fixtures, call `erg install --hooks` into the temp repo
  rather than maintaining a hand-rolled copy. No install.go parsing needed; the
  binary provides the hook text. Hermetic and offline: the dynamic default-branch
  detection falls back to "main" when no remote is configured, which is exactly
  the test environment -- behavior is stable without network. Regarding 0225: if
  0225 lands a reusable shell extraction helper, source it; if 0225 leaves guard
  (iv) inline (current state: test_selfcoherence.sh lines 86-94), no sharing is
  needed -- test_hook/roundtrip install the whole hook and assert behavior, not
  block content. Never parse install.go directly.
- Antipattern scan: tautological-test risk is NOT present -- these tests assert
  behavioral outcomes (commit reject/allow, round-trip file hygiene), not
  string-equality with hookBody. A logic bug in hookBody would still surface as a
  wrong accept/reject. The hookBody == documentation equality is separately owned
  by guard (iv) / ticket 0225. Division of labor is clean. No premature abstraction
  risk: 2-3 inline call sites, no existing sourced shell library; inline matches
  precedent.

## Plan (raid 2026-06-04)

### Actions

1. tests/test_hook.sh lines 1-4 (header): add ERG/ERG_ABS lines after line 4:
   ERG="${ERG_BIN:-build/erg}"
   ERG_ABS=$(CDPATH= cd "$(dirname "$ERG")" && pwd)/$(basename "$ERG")
   (mirrors test_install.sh:5-6 and test_roundtrip.sh:5)

2. tests/test_hook.sh line 27 (comment "# Install the hook fragment"):
   replace lines 27-41 (comment + mkdir + cat heredoc + HOOK + chmod) with:
   mkdir -p tickets
   cp "$ERG_ABS" tickets/erg
   mkdir -p .git/hooks
   "$ERG_ABS" install . --hooks >/dev/null
   The cp is the install precondition (install.go:181-186: binaryPath stat).
   install forces exec bits (readHookFile:370) so chmod is not needed.
   Invocation must be "$ERG_ABS" not "$ERG" because cd "$REPO" (line 18) changes
   directory and a relative ERG path would be unreachable.

3. tests/test_hook.sh line 43-45 (ELF stub block: comment + printf + chmod):
   replace with nothing -- the cp in Action 2 already placed the real binary
   at tickets/erg. Removing the stub is the sole purpose of this deletion.

4. tests/test_hook.sh lines 64-68 (Test 2 "make build" and "build/erg" assertions):
   drop the two grep blocks for "make build" (lines 64-67) and "build/erg"
   (lines 69-72). Replace with grep blocks for:
     "do not commit tickets/erg"   (install.go hookBody:89)
     "CI rebuilds the binary after merge"  (install.go hookBody:90)
   Keep the existing "no-verify" assertion (line 74-78) unchanged.
   Rationale: the branch-guard rejection path (install.go:88-92) never reaches
   the validate section and thus never emits "make build" or "build/erg". Those
   strings appear only on the binary-not-found path (install.go:109). Confirmed
   empirically: actual rejection output is "pre-commit: do not commit tickets/erg
   in feature branches." and "CI rebuilds the binary after merge. To override: git
   commit --no-verify".

5. tests/test_roundtrip.sh lines 34-53 (comment + cat heredoc + HOOK + chmod):
   replace with:
   "$ERG" install "$REPO" --hooks >/dev/null
   The test already cp's "$ERG" to "$REPO/tickets/erg" (line 29) before this
   block, satisfying the install precondition. "$REPO" is absolute. chmod is
   redundant (install forces exec bits). No erg init needed: empirically verified
   that "tickets/erg check tickets/" passes on a bare store with only tickets/erg
   present (no .ergrc, no AGENTS.md).

### Hermeticity notes

- Install invocability (install time): install.go:335-350 (resolveHooksDir) shells
  out to "git -C root rev-parse --git-path hooks" -- requires a git repo, no
  network. install.go:181-186 requires tickets/erg present. Both conditions are
  met before the call in both tests.
- Hook offline fallback (commit time, test_hook.sh Tests 1-3): install.go:85-86
  sets default_branch via git symbolic-ref (fails silently with no remote) and
  falls back to "main" via ${default_branch:-main}. In the temp repo with no
  remote the fallback fires, so the branch guard still rejects feature/test. This
  is the commit-time fallback, distinct from the install-time preconditions above.

### First test

Run make check-fast and observe that test_hook.sh and test_roundtrip.sh pass.
To prove failure: revert only Action 4 (keep "make build" assertion) and confirm
test_hook.sh Test 2 fails with "FAIL: feature branch: error message mentions make
build". To prove the ELF removal works: revert Action 3 only and confirm Test 4
passes (real validate+check runs with the real binary, not the stub that could not
exec).

### Dependencies

- build/erg must be built (make build) before running the affected tests. Both
  test_roundtrip.sh (line 5: ERG_BIN:-build/erg) and the new test_hook.sh header
  depend on it. No other ticket dependency: Action 2 uses install.go as-is (current
  HEAD); 0225 (guard iv inline vs. extracted helper) does not affect this ticket
  because test_hook.sh and test_roundtrip.sh assert behavioral outcomes, not block
  content equality.

### Tautology scan

No tautology risk. Tests assert accept/reject outcomes (commit allowed or blocked)
and round-trip file hygiene -- not string equality with hookBody. A logic error in
hookBody (e.g. wrong branch variable) would produce a wrong commit result and the
test would catch it. The only new string assertions (Action 4) check for two
substrings present in both the test's expectation and the shipped hook's rejection
path, but the hook itself is not the test oracle -- git commit's stderr is. Guard
(iv) in test_selfcoherence.sh owns the hookBody == integration.md equality check
separately. Division of labor is clean.

After the change, Test 4 is strictly more behavioral than before: the real binary
now executes "tickets/erg validate" and "tickets/erg check tickets/" during the
commit (hookBody:96-112), whereas the ELF stub was never invoked. A validate or
check regression would now surface here.
